{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 22, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Tripoli and ruled the County of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Toron. Raymond III was married to Eschiva of Bures and they had a son named Bohemond IV of Antioch.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nRaymond III was born in 1140 and succeeded his father in 1152. At the time of his succession he was only 12 years old and his mother Hodierna acted as regent. In 1157 he married Eschiva of Bures. \n\n**Military Campaigns**\n\nDuring his rule Raymond III fought against the Zengid dynasty of Aleppo led by Nur ad-Din. In 1164 he joined the army of the Kingdom of Jerusalem led by King Amalric I at the Battle of Montgisard where they defeated the Ayyubid forces led by Saladin. He also fought at the Battle of Marj Ayyun in 1179. \n\n* **Crusader Siege of Damascus**\nIn 1177 Raymond III participated in the Crusader Siege of Damascus alongside the army of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. However the siege was unsuccessful and the Crusaders were forced to retreat.\n\n**Death and Succession**\n\nRaymond III died in 1187 during the Battle of Hattin. He was succeeded by his son Bohemond IV of Antioch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00016938205}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0010648064}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1300828}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.349725e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00021371941}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.651657e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.015882885}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.34376433}, {"token": " member", "logprob": -0.5870414}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.3748852e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00829915}, {"token": " House", "logprob": -0.27775657}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -5.483477e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -1.098